1 OCCU Ärkebiskop (nr.39), teologie professor, Ärkebiskop
1 TITL Metropolitan Archbishop
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lars Stigzelius=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lars_Stigzelius '''Lars Matsson Stigzelius'''] was [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archbishop_of_Uppsala Archbishop of Uppsala] in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_Sweden Church of Sweden]
2 CONC  from 1670 to his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the son of''' a priest and was a student at the Uppsala University until his Master of Arts in 1625. After undertaking a travel through Europe in 1630, he in 1640 became professor of theology in Uppsala. During his time 
2 CONC as professor he was under pressure since both [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Skytte '''Johan Skytte'''], the chancellor of the university, and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurentius_Paulinus_Gothus '''Laurentius Paulinus 
2 CONC Gothus'''], the vice chancellor and a learnt professor who would later become archbishop, were supporters of the philosophy of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramism Ramism] (deriving from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrus_Ramu
2 CONC s Petrus Ramus]), while Stigzelius was an [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aristotle aristotelian].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This problem he had''' from 1630, when he became professor of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic logic], until, as said, 1640, when he became professor of theology. When in the 1660s [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ren%C3%A9_D
2 CONC escartes Cartesian] thoughts spread to the university, Stigzelius was working against it. He had a reputation at the University as being highly knowledgeable. His views usually counted. For instance he was working to remove [https
2 CONC ://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exorcism exorcism] as one of the Church dogmas (which still was in use in Sweden).
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
